  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MHPSS Gaza 2024 &#x2013; WHO MHPSS Technical Working Group Coordinator (MHPSS24PS1)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unrest in the State of Palestine has been on the rise in in the last six months, particularly in Gaza.In Gaza, the humanitarian consequences have been devastating, exacerbating the impact of almost 14 years of an Israeli blockade, internal Palestinian political divisions and recurrent escalations. With the recent escalation of the 7th of October, according to the World health Organization (WHO) situation report of the 2nd of April, 32,975 fatalities (72% are children and women) , 75,572 injured, 1.7 million people are displaced ( 75% of the total population) .10 out of 36 hospitals are partially functioning, 27 PHC (primary health care) facilities out of 89 are functional. 28 patients reportedly died of malnutrition. In northern Gaza 12.4%-16.5% of children (6-59 months) with acute malnutrition. In southern Gaza 2-6% of children with acute malnutrition. In addition, to the ongoing outbreaks of diarrheal illnesses and hepatitis A.The Ministry of Health&apos;s Mental Health department (MOH MH) services are not functional, there used to be six community MH centres and one psychiatric hospital, only one Community Mental Health Center (CMHC) in Rafah and two PHC centres providing MH support and psychotropics. The United Nations Relief and Works Agency (UNRWA) and local non-governmental organizations (NGOs) such as Gaza Community Mental Health Programme (GCMHP) are providing support in Rafah area too.</narrative>
  </description>
